{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\ned2b (`rebar show` intermittently returned EMPTY stdout with exit 0 under concurrent background auto-push) was fixed by bounding the read-path reconverge lock wait (`_RECONVERGE_LOCK_TIMEOUT = 2` in `src/rebar/_engine_support/reads.py`) and landed with a show-only regression test (`tests/interfaces/store/test_show_no_stall.py`). But read-output integrity under sync contention is a GENERIC property of every read surface that routes through `ensure_fresh` — list, search, ready, next-batch share the same reconverge path as show and would regress silently (bug-trend review change 20: one-time machinery, no bespoke per-surface copies).\n\n## Approach\nGeneralize the existing ed2b harness rather than inventing a new storm: reuse/hoist `repo_with_origin_tickets` + the `_rebar_cli` helper from `test_show_no_stall.py` into a sibling property module. One property-style test parameterized over the CLI read surfaces (`show`, `list`, `search`, `ready` at minimum): under the same burst-of-writes contention (each `rebar edit` spawning a background push via `REBAR_SYNC_PUSH=always`), every ZERO-exit read invocation must produce PARSEABLE output for its format. Run every surface with `--output json` and pin: exit 0 implies stdout parses as JSON of the surface's documented shape (list/object). This sidesteps legitimately-empty text output — e.g. `rebar ready` in default text mode prints nothing when no tickets are unblocked — because valid-empty serializes as `[]`, distinguishable from truncated-empty stdout. A LOUD nonzero exit is acceptable — empty-success is the bug. Explicitly NOT pagination invariants: rebar's read CLI has no cursor/offset pagination; the property is output-integrity-or-loud-error.\n\nThrottle handling (decisive): `ensure_fresh` reconverges at most 1/min per store via the `/tmp/.ticket-sync-<md5(tracker)>` marker, so only the first read in a window can stall. The harness must call the existing `_clear_sync_throttle(tracker)` helper (already in `test_show_no_stall.py:69`) BEFORE EACH parameterized read invocation so every surface actually exercises the reconverge path rather than short-circuiting to the local snapshot.\n\n## Scope\n- tests/interfaces/store/ — new sibling module + minimal fixture/helper hoist (no production code)\n\n## Testing\nThe test IS the deliverable. RED demonstration: temporarily revert the ed2b ledge locally (raise `_RECONVERGE_LOCK_TIMEOUT` back to the 15s writer default so reads stall on the held lock) and observe the property fail on at least one surface; restore and confirm green.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] One parameterized property covers show/list/search/ready via the real CLI under the ed2b write-burst + background-push harness; no bespoke per-surface copies.\n- [ ] Invariant pinned: exit 0 implies stdout parses as the surface's JSON shape (valid-empty `[]` passes; truncated/empty stdout fails); nonzero exits pass (loud failure allowed).\n- [ ] Throttle marker cleared before each read so every invocation exercises the reconverge path.\n- [ ] RED demonstrated by locally reverting the reads.py lock-timeout ledge; green on the fixed tree.\n- [ ] ed2b harness reused (hoisted or imported), not duplicated."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785724588202901001,"uuid":"36781839-a443-4b5c-9b4d-0734e85bec73"}